From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:18:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: port jtrefon TBQ3_0/TBQ4_0 at ids 58/59 with the
 type-id arbitration, plus the SET_ROWS device guard (WI-1694 half A)

TurboQuant TBQ3_0 (d + qs[48], signed FWHT + 8 Lloyd-Max centroids, 50 B / 128) and TBQ4_0 (d + qs[64], 16 centroids, 66 B / 128) land at ids 58 and 59 - retagged from the author's 42/43, which this tree already spends - per docs/TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md 3.1.3. CPU reference only in this lane: every backend without a kernel must report these as not supported, never a wrong value. License recorded in licenses/turboq-mtp-MIT.txt and licenses/README.md.

Opt-in by TYPE NAME: the types are reachable only by naming them (-ctk/-ctv tbq4_0), so no default moves and every launch that does not name one is byte-identical to the pre-commit engine. Two guards ride with them: LLAMA_ALLOW_TBQ3_KV (default OFF) refuses a tbq3_0 V cache, which the source fork measured collapsing into token repetition, and warns on tbq3_0 K; and a runtime DEVICE guard refuses a TBQ KV cache at context init when the offload device cannot run SET_ROWS into it, instead of letting the scheduler abort at graph time. Override the device guard the normal way: -nkvo, -dev none, or a supported type.

Union resolution against WI-1692 in this merge: the SX8 (57) and TBQ (58/59) rows, type_traits_cpu entries, ops.cpp case labels, ggml-quants.c row validators and test-backend-ops all_types entries are all KEPT SIDE BY SIDE - both mechanisms stay, nothing replaced. The stale "57 RESERVED" row this branch carried in TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md is dropped in favour of the implemented SX8 row.

